-- The ride seals put their rider on the animal.
--
-- A ride seal is ITEM_UNIQUE / UNIQUE_SPECIAL_RIDE (16/2), worn in a unique
-- slot. CHARACTER::EquipItem hands a worn one to the quests as sig_use on
-- QUEST_NO_NPC (CItem::IsOldMountItem, @fixme152), and the package ships no
-- quest that answers it, so a seal put on did nothing (23 September: not one
-- compiled quest object calls pc.mount). This one mounts the animal the seal
-- names. Taking the seal off, /unmount and the seal running out all end the
-- ride in the engine (CItem::ClearMountAttributeAndAffect), so the mount is
-- given for as long as the seal can last; the seal's own clock (value0 minutes,
-- counted by unique_expire_event only while it is worn - thirty hours, set by
-- the migrator's ItemShop mounts step) is what the rider pays in.
--
-- The four war seals, whose animals the world's mob_proto names: 20115 Dzik
-- Wojenny, 20116 Wilk Wojenny, 20117 Szarzujacy Tygrys, 20118 Waleczny Lew.
-- The other seals of the package wait for their animals to be read off the
-- world. Keep this list and ishop_seals in the migrator (migratorify.py) the same.
quest mount_seals begin
    state start begin
        -- A plain chain rather than a keyed table: it is the shape every
        -- shipped quest compiles, and qc's lexer is the one thing here that
        -- nobody could run before release.
        function mob_of(vnum)
            if vnum == 71125 then
                return 20115
            elseif vnum == 71126 then
                return 20116
            elseif vnum == 71127 then
                return 20117
            elseif vnum == 71128 then
                return 20118
            end
            return 0
        end

        when sig_use begin
            local mob = mount_seals.mob_of(item.get_vnum())
            if mob > 0 then
                pc.mount(mob, 60 * 60 * 24 * 365)
            end
        end
    end
end
